  "description": "Sizes may be temporarily unavailable as our frame stock sells out. More Montréal frames are currently in production in all sizes, with a tentative ETA of late spring.\nThis build of Le Montréal has long been our unofficial favourite, and you'll see many Montrealers cruising around their neighbourhoods on the previous editions of the Montréal built up just like this one, so we decided it was finally time to make it official. It's also ideal for weekend trips out of town and long commutes across the island, with a compact single-chainring transmission for a simple, useful range of gears without needing to go full racer.\nFirst released in 2013, Le Montréal has been our most popular frameset and our most versatile. Inspired by classic 1980s touring bikes, Le Montréal features eyelets for front and rear fenders and racks, three bottle cages, and our signature shoulder strap. The wheel size is proportional to the frame size, making the bicycle more comfortable and controllable for variously-sized riders. The stiffened seatstays and top-tube not only increase its load-carrying ability, they also contribute to adding some spring to its step.\nBuild Specs\n\nShimano/Microshift 1x8-speed transmission\nBassi narrow-wide crank (38t with chainguard) for simpler maintenance and comfortable gears\nSuper-tough city/touring wheels on Sun CR18 polished silver rims\n11-34t Microshift Cassette\nPuncture-resistant all-surface tires\nTektro 855AL extra-long v-brakes, fantastic braking power and loads of room for fenders and racks\n\nNew features for the Montréal V3\n\nOversized tubes on all sizes for better stability with a touring load (or your kid) on the rear of the bike\nExtra bottle cage mount under the downtube (that's three total)\nMore rooms for wide tires, up to 45mm on all sizes (with fenders!)\nReduced toe overlap by using three wheel sizes across the range, also making the bicycles more proportional to the rider for more pleasant handling\n\n46cm and 49cm for small riders use 26\" wheels\n52cm and 55cm for average riders use 650B (27.5\") wheels\n58cm and 61cm (our largest frame yet!) use 700C (28\") wheels\n\nA return to diagonal dropouts, for singlespeed fans\n\nM5 eyelets at mid-fork, on seat stays and drop-outs for rack and fenders\nThree bottle cage mounts\nEyelets on seat tube and top tube for shoulder strap\n\nGeometry\n\nFinal product may differ from image",
